          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+line+bundle"} universal complex line bundle
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly homotopy equivalent
            to the base space of the line bundle, hence to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+section"} zero section
            of the universal line bundle, followed by its inclusion into its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            (
            %a{:href => "#Adams74"}> Adams 74, Part I, Example 2.1
            , see Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheStatement"}
            below).
          %p
            This statement plays a key role in the discussion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology"} complex oriented cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+class"} universal
            first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+Chern+class"} Conner-Floyd Chern class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^E_1
            is equivalent to a choice of universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+class"} Thom class
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+line+bundle"} universal complex line bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
            %em
              %a{:href => "universal+complex+orientation+on+MU#ConnerFloydChernClassesAreThomClasses"} Conner-Floyd E-Chern classes are E-Thom classes
            for more on this.)
          %p In this context the statement is naturally stated in the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi M
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \mathrm{U}(1) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} M \mathrm{U}(1)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            is thought of as the component space in degree 2 (complex degree 1) of the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
          %p
            The analogous statement is true also for the universal
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundle"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+line+bundle"} quaternionic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+oriented+cohomology+theory"} quaternionic oriented cohomology theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi M
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B Sp(1) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} M Sp(1)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            is thought of as the component space in degree 4 (quaternionic degree 1) of the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+unitary+group"} quaternionic unitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSp"} MSp
          %h2#preliminaries Preliminaries
          %h3#the_universal_line_bundle The universal line bundle
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕂
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
